{
 "**Asking:** the two-finger double tap, the **Hint** action, or {{H}} on a keyboard. The hint is spoken, for example “Hint: slide red brick, row 1, column 3, left, out through its gate”, and VoiceOver moves to that piece.": "help:voiceover",
 "**Bold Text** and **Zoom** work everywhere in the game.": "help:vision-hearing-and-motion",
 "**Colour is never the only clue.** Colour-blind symbols are on from the start, and every brick, gate and goal can carry a shape. See [Vision, hearing and motion](help:vision-hearing-and-motion).": "help:accessibility",
 "**Colour-blind** is on from the very first board. Every brick is stamped with a shape for its colour, coloured specials wear a small shape badge, and the goals in the header carry the same shape, so you can match bricks to goals without telling colours apart.": "help:vision-hearing-and-motion",
 "**Every piece has a name.** VoiceOver reads a piece’s kind, colour and state, for example “Blue line blaster, horizontal, clears its row”, and a face-down brick never gives its colour away.": "help:accessibility",
 "**Extras follow the piece:** “in front of the red gate”, “red gate to the left”, “portal entrance below”, “counts for Daffodil, yellow” when a goal needs it. An empty cell says “Empty”.": "help:voiceover",
 "**Face-down bricks never tell you their colour:** “Face-down brick, turns over when a brick next to it leaves the board”. That is fair play, not a missing label.": "help:voiceover",
 "**Free:** a hint you ask for with the two-finger double tap or the action never uses a Hint booster from the tray.": "help:voiceover",
 "**Gates are their own elements,** for example “Red gate, 2 cells wide, left side, rows 3 to 4”, and their value says whether they are open, iced, need more bricks, or are closed for good.": "help:voiceover",
 "**Idle hints:** if you pause for a while, a quiet hint may be spoken without moving your focus.": "help:voiceover",
 "**Large Content Viewer:** at the largest sizes, touch and hold a control in the board header or tray to see a magnified label, then lift your finger.": "help:vision-hearing-and-motion",
 "**Larger Text:** in the iPhone **Settings › Accessibility › Display & Text Size › Larger Text**. Body text can grow to more than double its size, headings to almost twice, and layouts stack so nothing is cut off. Win and out-of-moves screens grow less, so they still fit.": "help:vision-hearing-and-motion",
 "**Move your way.** Slide or swap with a touch, with VoiceOver actions, by saying “Slide red 14 left”, with switches, or with the arrow keys.": "help:accessibility",
 "**Nothing depends on hearing.** Every sound in OutBrick has something on screen to match it. The friends speak in text bubbles, not voices, and VoiceOver announcements are spoken by your own VoiceOver.": "help:vision-hearing-and-motion",
 "**Nothing to hear that you cannot also see.** The friends talk in text bubbles, not voices, and every sound has something on screen to match it.": "help:accessibility",
 "**Pieces are named by kind, colour and state,** never by colour alone: “Red bomb”, “Crate, 2 layers”, “Yellow brick, locked, a line through it frees it”, “Red long brick, 2 tall”.": "help:voiceover",
 "**Row sound** (Settings › Accessibility) adds a **Hear row** action on the board: a short, quiet note for each piece from left to right, one pitch per colour symbol, with a different tone for round, pointed and straight shapes. Blockers make a low knock and empty cells are a rest.": "help:vision-hearing-and-motion",
 "**Settings › Accessibility › High-contrast board** draws the board on a near-black floor with a faint grid, puts a white outline on every piece and a large white symbol on plain bricks, and gives every gate a thick outline. Gate colours are checked against the floor, and a gate whose colour is too close to it gets a two-tone outline.": "help:vision-hearing-and-motion",
 "**Sounds, Music and Haptics** each have their own switch in **Settings › Game**, and in the Pause menu during a board. Haptics only appears on devices that can vibrate.": "help:vision-hearing-and-motion",
 "**The Board summary comes first.** It reads the level, its name, the stage, the goals and the moves left. Double-tap it to hear the whole board read out with a hint.": "help:voiceover",
 "**Then every cell, row by row,** from the top left. Gaps in a board’s shape are skipped. Each cell’s value is its place, for example “Row 3, column 2”.": "help:voiceover",
 "**Time to think.** No timers, an Animation speed setting from 50% to 200%, and an optional **Hold to confirm swaps** so nothing plays by accident.": "help:accessibility",
 "A board, top to bottom: the header, the grid, and the tray. VoiceOver reads the header’s summary first, then the grid row by row.": "help:voiceover",
 "A free hint. The best move shimmers and is spoken; your Hint booster is not used.": "help:voiceover",
 "A locked level says how far away it is: “4 more to unlock”.": "help:voiceover",
 "A solid dark floor, white outlines, large colour symbols and thick door outlines.": "help:accessibility",
 "A starting point for your needs": "help:accessibility",
 "A swap that makes nothing springs back and says “No match, swapped back. No move used”. You have lost nothing.": "help:voiceover",
 "Accessibility in OutBrick: start here": "help:accessibility",
 "Action": "help:voiceover",
