 "The Settings screen on the Accessibility tab. Animation speed is set to 100% with choices from 50% to 200%. Announcement detail is set to Standard, with Brief and Full either side. Below are on and off switches for Colour-blind (on), High-contrast board, Left-handed tray, Hold to confirm swaps and Row sound (all off).": "help:accessibility",
 "The actions on a piece, in the order you hear them": "help:voiceover",
 "The end: “Every goal done. Level complete” or “Out of moves”.": "help:voiceover",
 "The first time you meet a new idea, a short teaching card explains it. It is the only thing on screen while it shows: double-tap to start playing.": "help:voiceover",
 "The friends, flags and artwork keep their real colours.": "help:accessibility",
 "The same kind of board with the high-contrast look: a near-black floor, white outlines around every brick and large white symbols.": "help:vision-hearing-and-motion",
 "The symbols also turn on whenever the iPhone’s **Differentiate Without Color** or the game’s **High-contrast board** is on.": "help:vision-hearing-and-motion",
 "The tray at the foot of a board holds Pause on the left and the boosters and Undo on the right. **Left-handed tray** mirrors it, so the boosters sit under your left thumb and Pause moves to the right.": "help:voice-control-switch-control-keyboard",
 "The tray, right-handed (the default). Left-handed mirrors it.": "help:voice-control-switch-control-keyboard",
 "The two-finger double tap speaks the guide, for example “Garden City, 7 of 12 levels cleared. Next: level 8. 3 stars to the village reward.”": "help:voiceover",
 "There are two ways to move, and you can mix them.": "help:voiceover",
 "There is no timer anywhere. Slow the **Animation speed** and use hints whenever you like.": "help:accessibility",
 "There is no timer on any board, menu or event in OutBrick. Each board gives you a number of **moves**, and that is the only limit. A move only counts when it actually does something: a swap that makes no match springs back and does not use a move.": "help:accessibility",
 "These live in the iPhone or iPad **Settings** app under **Accessibility**, and OutBrick responds to them on its own.": "help:accessibility",
